  "input": {
    "id": "52827",
    "name": "Massaman Beef curry",
    "cuisine": "Thai",
    "instructions": "Heat oven to 200C/180C fan/gas 6, then roast the peanuts on a baking tray for 5 mins until golden brown. When cool enough to handle, roughly chop. Reduce oven to 180C/160C fan/gas 4.\r\nHeat 2 tbsp coconut cream in a large casserole dish with a lid. Add the curry paste and fry for 1 min, then stir in the beef and fry until well coated and sealed. Stir in the rest of the coconut with half a can of water, the potatoes, onion, lime leaves, cinnamon, tamarind, sugar, fish sauce and most of the peanuts. Bring to a simmer, then cover and cook for 2 hrs in the oven until the beef is tender.\r\nSprinkle with sliced chilli and the remaining peanuts, then serve straight from the dish with jasmine rice.",
